e/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040191/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c30abe1714a2799d7ccd35262b7446d948c8b200e0fcedf24f7363317265f2"} {"question" "q-80389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=6.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040191/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c30abe1714a2799d7ccd35262b7446d948c8b200e0fcedf24f7363317265f2"} {"question" "q-80389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4286a7677ab3c62ffb9e374117e194de0d203869cbdc668cbdd42a9e42c489bf"} {"question" "q-80389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040191/state.json" "file_sha256" "89c30abe1714a2799d7ccd35262b7446d948c8b200e0fcedf24f7363317265f2"} {"question" "q-80389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$D=[\\begin{al